# Nothing is pushed unless it is named below.
#
# The first line ignores everything; each `!` puts one thing back. A file that
# is not in this list cannot reach the repo by accident -- which makes this a
# manifest as much as a filter: it is the answer to "what does someone get when
# they clone this".
#
# Adding something is a line here. That is the cost of the arrangement, and the
# point of it: `git status` stays quiet until a file is meant to ship, and a
# stray download, a database, a compiled binary or a source file cannot end up
# on the other side of it by being nearby.
#
# Order matters. A folder is let back in first, then what lives inside it.
# `git check-ignore -v <path>` says which line decided any file.

*

# --- the front page and the paper trail ---
!.gitignore
!README.md
!COMMANDS.md
!LICENSE.MD
!CHANGELOG.md

# --- the compiler ---
!bin/
!bin/sintax

# --- the example program ---
!sin/
!sin/sin.stx
!sin/invite.txt

# --- every image it names, one line each ---
!sin/guest_bg.jpg
!sin/guest_header.jpg
!sin/login_good.jpg
!sin/reg_fail.jpg
!sin/reg_success.jpg
!sin/secret_door.jpg
!sin/user_exists.jpeg
!sin/wrong_pass.jpg
!sin/icon.png

# Not listed above, and so not shipped: sin/sin (what compiling sin.stx makes),
# sss.db (what running it makes), .DS_Store, and anything else that turns up in
# this folder. To carry a new asset, add its line and it appears in git status.
